{
  "about": "Remote access (docs/features/remote-access.md). `externalUrl`: what a typed domain becomes, or the reason code it is refused with — the server's PUT /api/server/external-url answers 422 with that code, and clients pre-check with the same rule. `probe`: a /api/status answer (null = no answer) against the nest's instanceId → verdict. `pick`: the address a client uses — candidates in order (primary, every lan, tailscale, external; duplicates dropped), first whose answer carries the nest's instanceId; `answers` maps an address to the instanceId it answered with (absent = no answer). Read by the server's tests/unit/test_remote_access.py, the renderer's next/remote tests, krobi-ios Tools/Checks and krobi-android ContratosTest. `reach`: the chosen route (null = infer: Tailscale detected → tailscale, a stored domain → domain, else local), the last proof from outside (`outside`: via + seconds ago, or null), whether Tailscale is detected and a domain stored, and the probe verdicts of the Tailscale and domain rows (null = not probed) → the status line's reach and detail and the chain's two links (state + word). `ago`: seconds → the words. `outsideVia` (server only): a request's client address against the nest's own networks and gateway → how it came in. Words are the rule's Spanish strings; a client may render the brand in «no es un nido de Krobi» through its own app-name constant.",
